---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<Base
  title="Corvelle - Support"
  description="How to get help with Corvelle: email the developer, or open an issue. Includes what to check when your iPhone will not pair with your server."
>
  <h1>Support</h1>
  <p>
    Corvelle is made by one developer. Both options below reach the same
    person. Use whichever you prefer.
  </p>

  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="mailto:corvelle@akitaka.me">corvelle@akitaka.me</a> - for
    questions, bugs, and feature requests. Use email if you do not want to post
    in public. In the app, Settings &rsaquo; About &rsaquo; Help opens a
    message to the same address.
  </p>

  <h2>Issue tracker</h2>
  <p>
    <a href="https://github.com/tarakanof/Corvelle-Site/issues">github.com/tarakanof/Corvelle-Site/issues</a>
    - public, and the better place for problems other users may also have.
    Please do not post your server's address, pairing code, or chat content
    there.
  </p>

  <h2>If your iPhone will not pair</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Corvelle needs a server you control. Check that the broker is running and
      that its address opens over <strong>https</strong> from the iPhone's
      network.
    </li>
    <li>
      Check the pairing code. If your broker asks an operator to approve new
      devices, the iPhone waits until the device is approved.
    </li>
    <li>
      If the app was paired before, sign out in Settings and pair again.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reporting something the assistant showed</h2>
  <p>
    Answers and Home blocks are written by your assistant and the AI model it
    uses, not by the developer. To report a block on Home, long-press it and
    choose <em>Report this block</em>. The email names the block, never its
    content. You can also remove it from Home in the same menu.
  </p>

  <h2>Privacy</h2>
  <p>
    The developer never sees your chats. See the
    <a href={`${base}/privacy/`}>privacy policy</a> for what goes where.
  </p>
</Base>
